        "thought_text": "The BFS implementation is correct, but there's an error in the condition for checking opposite parity. The condition should be (a[current] % 2) != (a[next_pos] % 2), but the code uses (a[current] % 2) != (a[next_pos] % 2) instead. Additionally, for positions with the same parity, the code should continue BFS without increasing distance, but it's adding the position to the queue with the same distance.",
